    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, whose elite sprint speed and favorable matchup against Merrill Kelly yield a team-high score of 82.13. By slotting into the leadoff spot against a favorable starter, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** maximizes his potential for run production and stolen base opportunities\u2014the latter being our primary organizational priority. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** remains a locked-in high-leverage asset with a score of 76.13; despite the dynamic platoon penalty for facing a lefty, his projected presence in the #3 hole combined with favorable wind conditions makes him the anchor of our infield production. **Lars Nootbaar** also earns a strong start (60.62) as his platoon advantage against Kevin Gausman offsets the difficulty of the matchup, securing his place as a reliable cornerstone for today\u2019s rotation.\n\nOur bench strategy reflects a conservative approach to game caps, with **Jacob Gonzalez** falling just short of our 40.0 threshold. While **Jacob Gonzalez** (42.41) cleared the floor numerically, the optimizer prioritized benching him due to the negative platoon variance against a tough Robbie Ray and the risk associated with a bottom-third batting order. **Dillon Dingler** (37.53) also failed to crack the active roster; despite a positive park factor, his negative platoon split against the right-handed Drew Rasmussen rendered him below our internal efficiency standards. \n\nManagers should monitor the statuses of **Junior Caminero**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Trea Turner**, as their scores are contingent on the confirmed lineups remaining consistent with our assumptions. We are particularly cautious regarding the matchups for **Kyle Schwarber** and **Trea Turner**, both of whom must contend with the high skill of Logan Gilbert. While the scores for **Colt Keith** (54.59), **Caleb Durbin** (57.43), **Chase Meidroth** (49.12), and **Pedro Ramirez** (55.55) place them firmly in the middle of our production tier, they are essential to maintaining the Zebras' offensive floor while we await the return of **Yordan Alvarez** and **Kazuma Okamoto** from their respective off-days.",
